<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chakrayudha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 800</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chakrayudha was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayudha-dynasty">Ayudha dynasty</a> around 800, installed by the Pala emperor Dharmapala in place of his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indrayudha">Indrayudha</a>. As a Pala client he submitted to the Rashtrakuta emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govinda-iii">Govinda III</a> during his northern campaign. He was later defeated by the Gurjara-Pratihara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagabhata-ii">Nagabhata II</a>, who took Kannauj and made it the Pratihara capital.</p></div>
